Here is the commit message:
genirq: devres: Fix testing return value of
 request_any_context_irq()

request_any_context_irq() returns a negative value on failure.
It returns either IRQC_IS_HARDIRQ or IRQC_IS_NESTED on success.
So fix testing return value of request_any_context_irq().

Also fixup the return value of devm_request_any_context_irq() to make it
consistent with request_any_context_irq().

Fixes: 0668d3065128 ("genirq: Add devm_request_any_context_irq()")
Signed-off-by: Axel Lin <axel.lin@ingics.com>
Reviewed-by: Stephen Boyd <sboyd@codeaurora.org>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/1431334978.17783.4.camel@ingics.com
Signed-off-by: Thomas Gleixner <tglx@linutronix.de>

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from incorrect handling of the return value of the `request_any_context_irq()` function. The original code checked if the return value was non-zero to determine failure, which is incorrect since the function returns negative values on failure. This led to potential misinterpretation of success or failure states in the IRQ request handling.

Here is the patch:
  */
 int devm_request_any_context_irq(struct device *dev, unsigned int irq,
 			      irq_handler_t handler, unsigned long irqflags,
 			      const char *devname, void *dev_id)
 {
 	struct irq_devres *dr;
 	int rc;

 	dr = devres_alloc(devm_irq_release, sizeof(struct irq_devres),
 			  GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!dr)
 		return -ENOMEM;

 	rc = request_any_context_irq(irq, handler, irqflags, devname, dev_id);
-	if (rc) {
+	if (rc < 0) {
 		devres_free(dr);
 		return rc;
 	}

 	dr->irq = irq;
 	dr->dev_id = dev_id;
 	devres_add(dev, dr);

-	return 0;
+	return rc;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(devm_request_any_context_irq);


